+# Persistent Todo HTTP Service
+
+A todo JSON API written with only the Python standard library.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+python3 server.py --port 8000 --file todos.json
+```
+
+- `--port`: port to listen on (default 8000)
+- `--file`: JSON file used for persistence (created/overwritten atomically on each mutation); existing state is loaded on startup
+
+The server binds to `127.0.0.1` by default and uses a threaded HTTP server, so concurrent requests are handled safely (state is guarded by a lock and persisted atomically via temp-file write + `os.replace`).
+
+## Endpoints
+
+| Method | Path | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| GET | `/health` | `{"status":"ok"}` |
+| GET | `/todos` | JSON array of todo items |
+| POST | `/todos` | Body `{"title":"text"}` → creates item `{"id":N,"title":"...","completed":false}`, returns 201. 400 on bad JSON or empty/invalid title. |
+| PATCH | `/todos/ID` | Body `{"completed":true}` → updates item, returns it. 400 on bad JSON/invalid payload, 404 on unknown id. |
+| DELETE | `/todos/ID` | Deletes item, returns 204. 404 on unknown id. |
+
+Any other path returns 404.
+
+## Examples
+
+```sh
+curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
+curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/todos
+curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/todos -d '{"title":"buy milk"}' -H 'Content-Type: application/json'
+curl -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/todos/1 -d '{"completed":true}'
+curl -X DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8000/todos/1
+```
+
+## Tests
+
+Integration tests start the server as a subprocess and exercise it over loopback HTTP:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v
+```
